A column schema.sql no longer makes would lose its values: refused, and
nothing changes. The error gives the step that drops it on purpose, and the
one that renames it.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 'hot');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
column `dish.note` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its values would go. Renamed? Add the step to ledger.sql: `ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN note TO <new name>;` Gone on purpose? `ALTER TABLE dish DROP COLUMN note;`
